AND THE CONSEQUENCE 106'S OWN AMENDMENT INTRODUCES AND DOES NOT TRACE
106 section 9.2 widens 'observable' to cover whether a value is produced.
98 section 3.2, citing 40 section 5.3, says a build arm may move an
unobservable coordinate and is FORBIDDEN to move an observable one.
I18's panic is moved by the build profile.
**Two costs of the inversion, stated rather than hidden.** Generating the section from a weighting means
the emitted arm selection can change between builds even with identical source. For an **unobservable**
coordinate that is licensed: `40` section 5.3 says an arm may resolve those however it likes and a later
arm may resolve them differently. For an **observable** one it is forbidden by the same section, so the
generation story applies exactly to the coordinates cost-based selection lives on, which is where it was
always meant to apply.

-- and the seam this lands on, which 102 already named as unnoticed --
155:  corpus is element count, width, arity, thread count and mode. A build condition is a `cfg`. A region is
156-  a property of the consumer's workload. These are disjoint sets of things and nothing has noticed.
157-- **Codomain.** `25` assigns values on headroom, packing, overflow and intermediate precision. `94`
158-  assigns an arm. An arm is a mechanism, so the codomains overlap, but only if every one of `25`'s axes
